Wait, that's a bug in my merge return value! Let me look:

```js
return this.#snapshotFrom([...this.#documents.values(), ...additions]);
```

`this.#documents.values()` — after merge, additions were already added to `this.#documents` (since !dryRun). So `[...this.#documents.values(), ...additions]` duplicates the additions! That gives 2 + 1 + 1 = 4.

Bug found. Fix: for non-dryRun, additions are already in #documents, so just snapshot #documents. For dryRun, additions are not in #documents, so include them.

```js
if (!dryRun) {
  for (const document of additions) this.#documents.set(document.id, document);
}
return this.#snapshotFrom(dryRun ? [...this.#documents.values(), ...additions] : [...this.#documents.values()]);
```

Or simpler:

```js
const merged = new Map(this.#documents);
for (const document of additions) merged.set(document.id, document);
if (!dryRun) this.#documents = merged;
return this.#snapshotFrom([...merged.values()]);
```

That's cleaner. Let me fix.

